Ryan Murphy you son of a [ __ ] you son  of a [ __ ] yes another season of  American Horror Story has come to an end  and I'll be perfectly honest I really  enjoyed it if you liked the campaign s  pardon the pun and if you're also like  me who grew up watching cheesy 80  slasher movies this season was such a  fun homage to those films I would even  put this season in my top 3 yes I know  that statement will automatically get me  some dislikes that being said the ending  although good was not great leaving a  lot to be desired both plot and  character wise so in this video I'm  gonna go over how American Horror Story  1984 should have ended now before we get  into this new ending we have to go over  an important ground rule episode one to  eight will remain unchanged this isn't  because I think they're perfect that's  not the case at all it's just that if I  started cherry-picking things here and  there to change this video would get  super complicated and I want to avoid  that now that we've got that out of the  way we need to focus on those aspects of  the finale that I think need to be  changed and I'll focus more on broad  criticisms than nitpicking minor things  like oh I wish Xavier had more air time  I see you Cody fern fans out there  my three main criticisms are as follows  one the curse of camp redwood was never  fully explored or resolved to some of  the most important character arcs namely  Brooke and Ricky were deeply  unsatisfying and finally the lack of  tie-ins to other AHS seasons the curse  of camp redwood is an enigma to me with  rules that seem to switch episode to  episode in order for certain plot points  to be hit by the writers like how long  does it take for a body to resurrect  that kind of changes throughout the  season how can Lavinia seemingly  teleport  where did jingles go at the end of  episode 8 for now let's focus on what we  do know about this curse and build our  ending around that one it started in  1948 with the death of bobbie richter  and her mother's subsequent murder spree  resulting in benjamin killing his own  mother this is why we don't have any  super old-timey ghosts which would hint  that the curse goes way before 40  after the massacre and death of Lavinia  anyone killed within the camp redwood  property is resurrected as a ghost for  all eternity it's essentially their own  limbo in the current ending there's no  real resolution to this curse when I  think there should be if Lavinia gets  Bobby back and patches things up with  Ben the curse theoretically should be  lifted but the ending we got the campers  were still stuck at redwood we'll get to  how I'll change this in a bit character  arcs were also a big problem for me  mainly those of Brooke and Ricky Brooke  starts off the season as our main  protagonist yet the final episode has  her hiding away marrying a dermatologist  and her only real purpose in the episode  is to exposition dump everything that  happened to her since 1989  Ricky although he doesn't have quite an  arc since his character is pretty static  throughout the season didn't get an  ending worthy of his evil character by  that I mean he could have gotten it a  lot worse now I don't mean physically  since his death was quite brutal but  emotionally an emotional betrayal of  sorts by someone he admires more than  anyone else we'll get to that too  and finally the ending missed some great  opportunities to tie in previous HS  seasons HS is known for connecting tons  of characters from different seasons to  one another and I think they could have  exploited this much more particularly  Ricky's relationship to Satan tying in  to apocalypse okay you've heard my  critiques now I'm gonna show you how I  think this season should have ended keep  in mind my ending is Patchett insane but  hey so was the season it likely has its  own problems I wrote this in a day and  it likely wouldn't happen due to well  you'll just have to keep watching let's  get into it we start just like the  original ending a grown up Bobby Richter  has arrived at Camp redwood in 2019  searching for answers about his father  whereas the original has him meet  Montana and Trevor in my version he  meets jingles his dad one of the things  I didn't like about the original was  that Bobby and jingles hug once and  that's about it  in my way it allows them to connect a  bit more before they big finale so that  when things finally get resolved we feel  more attached to them and it's more  emotional less forced well jingles will  go on to say that he and the other  ghosts are stuck for it  Trinity at Camp redwood their souls will  never be at rest the curse was supposed  to be lifted when Lavinia was reunited  with Bobby but some evil force is  preventing the ghosts aka the other  campers and counselors from moving on  it's here the other ghosts reveal  themselves to Bobby as we flash back to  1989 to hear the story of what happened  at the festival Trevor will block the  road preventing the festival goers from  getting in but it's here none other than  Billy Idol arrives in his tour bus  played of course by Evan Peters but  someone else should he not be available  he's flown all the way from the UK and  is pissed  what do you mean the festival's canceled  he gave up a meeting with the Queen to  be here will he still be getting paid he  storms past Trevor on to the camp  redwood grounds in search of Margaret  demanding answers I like this version  because the original built up Billy Idol  for almost three episodes and there was  no payoff Billy can also be used  plot-wise to manipulate Ricky since we  know how much he loves him Montana will  exploit this by telling Ricky she's  arranged a private meeting with him away  from all the other less devoted fans and  this could take place in Lavinia Shack  where the other ghosts wait for him  trapping him in there similar to the  original we flash forward back to  present day where jingles brings his son  to see Ricky who they have tied up and  confined in his own satanic cell for the  past 30 years this scene could be fun  since you'll have Ricky taunting Bobby  saying he'll get his revenge and saying  how he enjoyed carving up his mother but  the real purpose of this scene is to  highlight how whatever satanic power is  trapped within Ricky is preventing the  curse from being lifted the ghosts have  tried everything but Ricky keeps coming  back to life with his satanic spirit  trapped within him if they can somehow  remove this demonic force from his body  maybe they can break the curse  in the mean time they've done the only  thing they can keep him confined so he  can't escape red wood  Bobby is now determined he says he'll  find a way to lift the curse and save  the other ghosts after all it was his  father and the other ghosts who have  been protecting him in the world all  these years from the evil that is Ricky  it's the least  can do jingles tells Bobby to start his  quest with Donna chambers at the red  Meadows Asylum she may have some answers  Bobby visits Donna at the asylum similar  to how he did in the original here we'll  have Donna recount how Brook and her got  the revenge and killed Margaret but my  version has an injured Brook being taken  to the camps edge by Ray only for her to  be saved by none other than Billy Idol  whose tour bus is still there as we  flash-forward Bobby says he thought  Brooke didn't survive he searched  everywhere for a Brooke Thompson but  couldn't find one that's because she's  no longer Brooke Thompson are you ready  for this she's Brooke Idol yes the girl  who started as a virgin with the  squeaky-clean lifestyle has come full  circle marrying one of the most badass  singers in rock and roll  a marriage that would have had to be  kept secret since Brooke is still  considered to be dead from death row  Bobby goes to the gates outside Billy's  mansion and is turned away by the guard  who thinks he's a crazy fan shouting  things about ghosts and camp redwood  kind of like how he was turned away at  the asylum but Brooke will overhear this  and bring him inside where Bobby will  plead with her to go back they need to  save the others and stop Ricky for good  the curse of Redwood needs to be lifted  and he doesn't know who to turn to  back at redwood a few days later Chet  and birdy are on the night shift looking  after Ricky just like the original when  they are viciously murdered by none  other than Billy Idol but as we'll find  out spoiler alert this is all part of  the plan it's not a big deal to kill  Chet and birdy since they'll just  resurrect again Ricky is astonished to  see his true hero helping him out of his  confinement Billy saying that Satan  talked to him and ordered him to set  Ricky free that Satan isn't done with  him Billy tells them a boat is waiting  for them at the dock and that they'll  finally be free once they get off the  property  as they get down to the dock Ricky  remarks where's the boat but it's all a  trap revealing cordelia at the other end  of the dock yes the cordelia good from  coven and apocalypse if there's anyone  who can deal with satanic beings it's  her and you know I had to bring our girl  Paulson back as we'll find out Billy is  actually a warlock who attended  Hawthorne hence how he would know  Cordelia and we could also tie this into  his success as  a rockstar Cordelia will cast a spell  lifting Ricki into the air as the  demonic spirit escapes from his throat  and mouth the other ghost from the  season emerge from the forest watching  as these events unfold including both  Bobby jingles Lavinia and Bobby jr. all  side by side with a final blow the  demonic entity is destroyed  casting the entire lake and forest in  bright white light  Ricky's body collapsing on the edge of  the dock the curse has been lifted and  Ricky is now mortal Billy takes Ricky's  curved knife ready to end him for good  it's the biggest betrayal for Ricky his  hero being the one to kill him when  Brooke swerves in and guts him in the  stomach after all it was Ricky who first  tried to kill her in episode 1 with  blood coming out from his mouth his face  of betrayal turns to an evil smirk as he  recites Billy's lyrics from his song  rebel yell saying more more MORE as  Montana and the other ghost stabbed him  mercilessly we get a goodbye between  jingles and Bobby before a mysterious  force slowly pulls the ghost towards the  center of the lake Cordelia Bobby Brooke  and Billy watch as the ghosts disappear  above the lake their souls finally put  to rest and the curse of red would  finally lifted I would have loved to  have months working on a better ending  than this one but hey with a half day  and not having to worry about whether  Evan Peters or Sarah paulsen could come  back I thought this would be a fun  exercise for all of us AHS fans out  there if you enjoyed it I would love it  if you gave it a like and made a comment  and make sure to subscribe since I have  tons of other videos coming up before  - HS season you can also follow me on  twitter at things story YT until next  time remember daddy loves you very much
 

